        <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p><i>Last Updated: November 18, 2026</i></p>

        <p>By inviting OnlyOneMessage or using its functionality, you agree to this Privacy Policy. 
        As mentioned in our Terms of Service, this policy may be updated at any time, including additions, removals, or edits to how data is handled.</p>

        <h3>1. Information We Collect</h3>
        <p>To ensure OnlyOneMessage functions properly, we collect and temporarily store the following data:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Server ID</b> - Used to identify and associate configurations with your server.</li>
            <li><b>Configured Channels</b> - Used to detect and process messages in configured channels.</li>
            <li><b>Member IDs</b> - Used for extended slowdown functionality.</li>
            <li><b>Configurations</b> - Configurations made from the <code>/config</code> and <code>/configchannel</code> commands.</li>
            <li><b>Usage Telemetry</b> - Anonymous and temporary data about feature usage, used only for performance insights and improvement.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2. How We Use Your Information</h3>
        <p>The information collected is used exclusively to operate and improve OnlyOneMessage. 
        We do not sell, rent, or share any data with third parties for advertising or marketing purposes. 
        All data handling is limited to what is necessary for the bot's functionality.</p>

        <h3>3. Data Retention</h3>
        <p>We retain collected data only as long as needed for the bot to operate. 
        Temporary data, such as Member IDs for Automatic Unblacklist, is automatically deleted after a maximum of 1 month. 
        Usage telemetry is anonymized and discarded once the bot session ends.</p>

        <h3>4. Data Security</h3>
        <p>All data collected by OnlyOneMessage is securely stored in <i>MongoDB</i>, a trusted and industry-standard database system. 
        Access to this data is restricted to the developers responsible for maintaining the bot. 
        Although the stored data is non-sensitive, we still take measures to prevent unauthorized access or data loss.
        While we take reasonable precautions to ensure data safety, no method of storage or transfer is entirely risk-free, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

        <h3>5. Your Rights & Data Removal</h3>
        <p>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your data at any time. 
        To request deletion of your data, you must remove OnlyOneMessage from your server. This will initiate an automated process to delete all associated data immediately.
        Additionally, you can contact us via our <a href="/support">Support Server</a> or email us at <a href="mailto:me@as2bax.dev">me@as2bax.dev</a>.</p>

        <h3>6. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h3>
        <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated occasionally to reflect new features or legal requirements. 
        When updates occur, they will be announced in our Support Server under <strong>#announcements</strong> and the “Last Updated” date above will be updated. 
        We encourage our users to review this page periodically to stay informed about our data practices.</p>
